I was just trying to have some fun!

257
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:52,220
You have my word! It's me!

258
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:53,920
I'm Joseph Joestar!

259
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,740
I was born September 27th in 1920!

260
00:18:57,280 --> 00:19:00,700
My wife's name is Suzy Q, and
I collect comics as a hobby!

261
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:03,620
I have a question for you.

262
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:06,984
Who's the leading actress
in Tarzan the Ape Man?

263
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:08,020
Bo Derek!

264
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,097
Okay, now answer this one.

265
00:19:10,180 --> 00:19:12,297
Who sang Eat It, the spoof of Beat It?

266
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:13,940
Weird Al Yankovic!

267
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:15,180
Good grief.

268
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:16,500
It has to be you.

269
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,327
Who else would know
pointless crap like that?

270
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:21,660
This is Card, over!

271
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,800
It's amazing! Mr.

272
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:25,352
Joestar is back with us!

273
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:27,777
He's come back from the brink of death!

274
00:19:27,860 --> 00:19:29,820
It's a miracle! Over!

275
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,580
Hear that?

276
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:35,646
We've taken back everything
you stole from us.

277
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:36,860
Do you?

278
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:07,900
It's finally over.

279
00:20:13,660 --> 00:20:16,440
Dio took something
precious from all of us.

280
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:19,740
For a hundred years, he's
taken whatever he wanted.

281
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:23,200
His appetite for power
has been insatiable.

282
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:25,900
He's taken far too much.

283
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,280
You realize that?

284
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:32,959
Yeah, he's taken things from us that
we'll never be able to get back.

285
00:20:33,960 --> 00:20:38,784
The losses that we've endured on this
journey stretch as far as the planet itself.

286
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:41,997
But thanks to their sacrifices,

287
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:45,520
we're here to tell the tale
and carry on in their stead.

288
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:52,620
Kakyoin. Iggy. Avdol.

289
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:55,040
It's over.

290
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:08,862
So you're really going
back to France, Polnareff?

291
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:13,160
This may be a bit forward,
but your family's gone.

292
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:16,128
Why don't you come back
with me to New York?

293
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:18,910
Mr.

294
00:21:18,993 --> 00:21:23,033
Joestar, I know they're gone, but
France is the only home I've ever known.

295
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,969
It's filled with memories.

296
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:28,280
It's a place I must return
to no matter where I go.

297
00:21:29,040 --> 00:21:30,805
But if you ever need anything,

298
00:21:30,980 --> 00:21:34,509
all you have to do is call and
I'll be there in a heartbeat.

299
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:36,687
We're gonna miss you, buddy.

300
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:43,940
It wasn't easy, that's for damn sure.

301
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,617
But I had a hell of a time,

302
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:50,171
and I'm lucky to have been on
this adventure with you guys.

303
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:55,840
Remember, we're a team, and
that's never gonna change.

304
00:21:57,360 --> 00:22:00,713
Calling all passengers for
France International Airlines.

305
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,100
Flight 92 to Paris.

306
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:04,220
Please proceed to gate 18.

307
00:22:04,820 --> 00:22:06,640
Avianto, you ornery bastard.

308
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:08,116
Live long and happy.

309
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:11,640
And you as moody grandson,
you'd better not forget me.

310
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:12,900
We'll meet again.

311
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:16,017
That is, of course, if you
don't hate my guts by then.

312
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,297
Stubborn jackass.

313
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:21,674
We wouldn't be able to forget about
you, even if we wanted to, Polnareff.

314
00:22:21,760 --> 00:22:22,900
You be well.

315
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,040
Au River.

316
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:27,490
Yeah.

317
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:28,820
See you later.

318
00:22:44,900 --> 00:22:45,730
Holly!

319
00:22:45,813 --> 00:22:47,857
How are you sitting up
straight all of a sudden?

320
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,800
I'm feeling much better.

321
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:52,455
I'm not sure how to put it into words.

322
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:54,877
It's as if we could
read each other's minds.

323
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:55,790
What?

324
00:22:55,873 --> 00:22:58,285
Mom, I can feel that
they're coming home to us.

325
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:01,800
Oh, Polly!

326
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:04,180
Papa and my Jotaro!

327
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:07,320
They're coming home!

328
00:24:00,280 --> 00:24:01,980
Thank you.

329
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:35,060
Thank you.
